Description: A tidy interface for population genetic clustering. This package
   provides a unified workflow to estimate, compare, summarize, and
   visualize genetic clustering analyses, supporting both single runs and
   collections of replicate analyses. It is designed to work natively with
   diploid and pseudohaploid data, and integrates seamlessly with the
   tidypopgen ecosystem. The package includes native R/C++ implementations of the 
   ancestry estimation method of ADMIXTURE (Alexander et al. 2009), using a
   modified version of the algorithm of OpenADMIXTURE (Ko et al. 2023),
   adapted to operate directly on the backing files of tidypopgen objects
   while correctly handling pseudohaploid data, and extended with the
   cross-validation of ADMIXTURE, and of
   the cluster-alignment method of clumppling 
   (Liu, Kopelman & Rosenberg 2024), ported with modifications from its
   python implementation, for the comparison of multiple clustering runs. Optionally, tidygenclust can also run external clustering
   software, including fastmixture, ADMIXTURE and ADAMIXTURE, which are installed 
   automatically in a dedicated conda environment (the conda environment only
   works in Linux and macOS).
